{
  "$comment": [
    "Splash's fee vectors: Amendment A1 section 3, every row, in one file.",
    "scripts/gen-fee-tests.mjs turns each row into a #[test] in move/splash_core/tests/fee_vectors_tests.move, which calls address_registry::derive_kind and fee_config::splash_fee on the launch schedule; tests/fee-schedule.test.mjs runs the same rows through lib/fees/schedule.ts. Edit this file, then run `node scripts/gen-fee-tests.mjs`; check:fees fails until the Move file matches.",
    "Amounts are USDC minor units (6 decimals), written as decimal strings so no row loses precision as a JSON number.",
    "kind: the kind the chain CHARGES, by A1's numbers (see kinds). declared: what the payer declares (default: kind). partner: the recipient is in the partner deposit-address registry (default: true when kind is BANK_PAYOUT). The recipient is a registered business wallet when kind is SPLASH_BUSINESS, and the payment goes through CCTP when kind is CROSS_CHAIN. discount_bps: the business's discount (0: none).",
    "Each expected fee was checked by hand against A1 sections 2.2 and 2.4: the tier by principal (upper bounds exclusive), less the discount, principal * bps / 10000 rounded down, then the kind's minimum and maximum, then the 100 bps ceiling."
  ],
